  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cocoa processing study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands has chosen cocoa as a focus sector in Ghana, in order to do less, but to do it better and more flexible in a systems approach. Cocoa is the sector in Ghana that should benefit from the prioritised combination approach of aid and trade instruments. In order to contribute to increasing the share in the value of cocoa flowing to the producing countries, there&#x2019;s the need to add value in country, either by indigenous processing companies or foreign direct investments in origin countries. This call is in line with the growing trend of local value addition in the region which presents an opportunity for Ghana to earn more from the cocoa trade while creating jobs for youth as well as opportunities for Dutch processors.</narrative>
  </description>
